# Autonomous issue agent — SHARED config TEMPLATE.
# Copy to config/shared.env (gitignored) and fill in. `bin/point-at.sh` sources
# config/shared.env FIRST, then overlays config/repos/<name>.env (per-repo wins).
# Never put a REPO/TARGET_DIR here — those live in the per-repo overlay.
#
#   cp config/shared.example.env config/shared.env   # then edit
#
# Repo-independent knobs only: GitHub App identity, identities, and runtimes.

# ── GitHub App identity (review runs as the App bot) ───────────────────────────
# The reviewer acts as a GitHub App, NOT a PAT — GitHub rejects a review
# approval from the same identity that authored the PR (422 self-approval), and an
# App gives a clean second bot identity with short-lived (~hourly) auto-minted
# tokens instead of a long-lived PAT.
#
# One-time setup:
#   1. Create a GitHub App (org-level). Permissions: pull_requests:write,
#      issues:write, contents:read, metadata:read.
#   2. Generate + download its private key (.pem); point GH_APP_KEY_FILE at it.
#   3. Install the App on the target org/repo; grab the installation ID.
#   4. Fill the three values below. REVIEW_BOT defaults to
#      my-reviewer-bot[bot] — only set it if your App has a different name.
GH_APP_ID="<your-app-id>"
GH_APP_INSTALL_ID="<your-installation-id>"
GH_APP_KEY_FILE="$HOME/.config/<your-app>/private-key.pem"
# GH_APP_TOKEN_CACHE defaults to ~/.local/state/issue-agent-bot/app-token.json.

# ── Identities ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fixer = ambient `gh auth` login (YOUR github user or a PAT). FIX_BOT MUST
# differ from REVIEW_BOT (the 422 self-approval rule).
#
# IDENTITY_MODE="solo" needs NONE of this: the review daemon is inert and
# auto-merge is structurally disabled, so the fixer opens PRs a human reviews.
# That is the recommended FIRST run — see docs/open/2026-07-26-first-run-handover.md.
#
# For "three", the second identity resolves in this priority (app/main.py
# `_app_identity`):  GitHub App token → static bot token → ambient gh auth.
# So there are TWO supported ways to get a reviewer, not just the App:
#
#   PATH A — bot user account + PAT. Simplest; no App. Create a second GitHub
#     account (ToS permits one machine account), invite it to the repo with
#     WRITE access, accept the invite, then issue it a fine-grained PAT with
#     Pull requests: R+W, Issues: R+W, Contents: R, Metadata: R. Set the two
#     lines below. REVIEW_BOT is the bare LOGIN — the `[bot]` suffix belongs to
#     Apps only. The token is long-lived, so keep this file 0600.
#   # REVIEW_BOT="your-bot-login"
#   # REVIEW_BOT_TOKEN="github_pat_..."
#
#   PATH B — GitHub App (the GH_APP_* block above). Short-lived ~hourly minted
#     tokens, so no long-lived secret on disk; prefer it once the loop is
#     proven. Its login carries the suffix: `my-app-name[bot]`. REVIEW_BOT
#     then defaults to the App login, so the App key + FIX_BOT is
#     enough and the line below can stay commented.
#
# The FIXER's credential is FIX_BOT_TOKEN or NOTHING — neither PATH A nor the
# App covers it. Leave it unset and the fix daemon falls through to ambient
# `gh auth`: every branch, comment and PR is attributed to that human account
# and the fixer spends that account's 5,000-point/hour GraphQL pool (keifu,
# 2026-08-02 — exhausted twice, harness blind ~50 min/hour). `issue-agent doctor`
# reports it, with the estimate.
IDENTITY_MODE="three"
FIX_BOT="<your-gh-login>"
# FIX_BOT_TOKEN="github_pat_..."
# REVIEW_BOT="my-reviewer-bot[bot]"

# ── Fixer runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "claude" = Claude Agent SDK (default, simplest). "codex" = OpenAI Codex CLI
# (needs `codex` on PATH + an OPENAI_API_KEY that authenticates to your gateway).
FIXER_RUNTIME="claude"
# Low/Med/High/XHigh implementer tiers; blank uses the selected runtime's
# built-in ladder. FIX_MODEL must be blank to enable difficulty routing.
FIX_MODEL_LOW="codex:gpt-6-luna"
FIX_MODEL_MED="codex:gpt-6.1-sol"
FIX_MODEL_HIGH="claude:claude-opus-5-5"
FIX_MODEL_XHIGH="codex:gpt-6-astra"
# For codex, point at your OpenAI-compatible gateway and model:
# OPENAI_API_KEY="${OPENAI_API_KEY:-}"
# OPENAI_BASE_URL="https://your-gateway/v1"
# CODEX_ENV_KEY="OPENAI_API_KEY"
# CODEX_BASE_URL="${OPENAI_BASE_URL}"
# CODEX_MODEL="<your-model-slug>"

# ── Reviewer runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Codex is the default reviewer runtime. Keep REVIEW_BOT as a separate GitHub
# App/token identity: runtime selection never changes GitHub's 422 self-approval
# rule. `REVIEW_BUDGET_USD` is enforced from trusted usage when both price rates
# are configured. The legacy CODEX_COST_PER_MTOK_* rate card is also the
# synthetic fallback for Claude/GLM subscription runs whose provider reports
# no billed cost, so armed aggregate caps cannot silently reset to zero.
#
# Mixed runtimes are recommended for self-hosting: setting REVIEWER_RUNTIME=claude
# while FIXER_RUNTIME=codex (or the inverse) preserves diversity, so one runtime
# regression cannot both create and approve the same failure.
REVIEWER_RUNTIME="codex"
REVIEW_MODEL="gpt-5.6-terra"
# Existing overlays that omit REVIEWER_RUNTIME adopt this default on their next
# launch. Set REVIEWER_RUNTIME="claude" (and optionally REVIEW_MODEL) before
# upgrading if Codex credentials are not configured or you want the mixed mode.

# ── LLM credentials (Anthropic) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any Claude-runtime fixer/reviewer drives Claude using YOUR
# Anthropic auth — the daemons inherit the launching shell's environment. Prefer
# exporting these in that shell (they're operator/machine-level, not repo config):
#   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...                       # direct API key, OR
#   export ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=... ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway
# If no ANTHROPIC_* env is set, the SDK falls back to your interactive `claude`
# login (~/.claude/.credentials.json). Either way it bills your own account/quota.
